 "summary": {
  "headline": "Credo Brands (Mufti) Q1 FY27 revenue rose 5% YoY to INR125.3 crore, but EBITDA fell to INR26.6 crore (21.2% margin) on higher marketing spend.",
  "overview": "Q1 FY27 revenue grew 5% YoY to about INR125 crore while gross margin was about 62% (61.6% per CFO). EBITDA was about INR27 crore versus about INR31 crore a year earlier, reflecting higher advertising, brand-building and retail transformation spend. PAT was INR2.3 crore (1.8% margin). Management said demand was healthy through April and part of May but moderated from mid-May, and it remains measured on near-term demand.",
  "financial_highlights": [
   {
